course: dictionary
lesson: 12756
title: Proper nouns: place names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proper noun is the special name of one person, place or thing. It always starts with a capital letter. Durham is the name of a particular place, so it begins with a big D.
explain: «We visited Durham last summer to see the cathedral.» Durham is one named city, not just any city, so it needs a capital letter. The word after «to» tells you it is a place, because you visit places.
explain: Check by asking: is this the name of one special thing? If yes, give it a capital letter. Durham is also used for a county and for places in other countries, but the capital letter stays the same.
fact: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Durham is a city in north-east England, famous for its very old cathedral and castle on a hill above the river Wear.
fact: Durham is also a university city, and the county around it is called County Durham.
fact: There is another Durham, a city in North Carolina, USA, and a region in Ontario, Canada.
fact: Durham can also be a surname, and it is the name of an old breed of shorthorn cattle (this is rare).
exercise: Why does Durham start with a capital letter in «We went to Durham to see the castle»? | *It is the name of one special place | It is always the first word in a sentence | It is a feeling | It is a word for a kind of animal
exercise: «The cathedral in Durham is very old.» What kind of place is Durham in this sentence? | A feeling of being happy | A type of cake | A river that flows into the sea | *A city in north-east England
exercise: Which sentence uses Durham correctly? | *Our school trip was to Durham, a city with a famous cathedral. | Our school trip was to durham, a city with a famous cathedral. | We visited durham castle on Monday. | We went to the durham and ate lunch.
test: Which river flows past the castle and cathedral in Durham? | Severn | Trent | *Wear | Thames
test: Which word is a proper noun for a place? | university | dog | *Durham | castle
exam: Which statement about Durham is correct? | It must always be written in small letters | It is only an old word for a castle | *It is a proper noun, so it begins with a capital letter | It is a verb meaning to walk slowly
